The main entry point of Wanchain cross-chain asset transfer system.      The contract serves as a gateway for cross-chain transactions between different blockchain networks. ","events":{"Initialized(uint8)":{"details":"Triggered when the contract has been initialized or reinitialized."},"RoleAdminChanged(bytes32,bytes32,bytes32)":{"details":"Emitted when `newAdminRole` is set as ``role``'s admin role, replacing `previousAdminRole` `DEFAULT_ADMIN_ROLE` is the starting admin for all roles, despite {RoleAdminChanged} not being emitted signaling this. _Available since v3.1._"},"RoleGranted(bytes32,address,address)":{"details":"Emitted when `account` is granted `role`. `sender` is the account that originated the contract call, an admin role bearer except when using {AccessControl-_setupRole}."},"RoleRevoked(bytes32,address,address)":{"details":"Emitted when `account` is revoked `role`. `sender` is the account that originated the contract call:   - if using `revokeRole`, it is the admin role bearer   - if using `renounceRole`, it is the role bearer (i.e. `account`)"}},"kind":"dev","methods":{"batchSetBaseFees(uint256[],uint256[])":{"details":"Function for the WMB Gateway contract, to be used by the contract administrator. These functions are only accessible to accounts with the DEFAULT_ADMIN_ROLE."},"dispatchMessage(uint256,address,bytes)":{"details":"Public interface functions for the WMB Gateway contract."},"dispatchMessageBatch(uint256,(address,bytes)[])":{"details":"This function is used to dispatch a batch of messages to a specified chain and returns a unique identifier for the dispatched batch.","params":{"messages":"An array of Message struct objects containing the destination addresses and data to be sent to each destination contract.","toChainId":"The chain ID of the destination chain."},"returns":{"messageId":"A unique identifier for the dispatched batch."}},"estimateFee(uint256,uint256)":{"details":"Estimates the fee required to send a message to a target chain","params":{"gasLimit":"Total Gas limit for the message call","targetChainId":"ID of the target chain"},"returns":{"fee":"The estimated fee for the message call"}},"getRoleAdmin(bytes32)":{"details":"Returns the admin role that controls `role`. See {grantRole} and {revokeRole}. To change a role's admin, use {_setRoleAdmin}."},"grantRole(bytes32,address)":{"details":"Grants `role` to `account`. If `account` had not been already granted `role`, emits a {RoleGranted} event. Requirements: - the caller must have ``role``'s admin role. May emit a {RoleGranted} event."},"hasRole(bytes32,address)":{"details":"Returns `true` if `account` has been granted `role`."},"receiveBatchMessage(bytes32,uint256,address,(address,bytes)[],uint256,bytes32,bytes,bytes32)":{"details":"Receives a message sent from another chain and verifies the signature of the sender.","params":{"gasLimit":"Gas limit for the message call","messageId":"Unique identifier of the message to prevent replay attacks","messages":"Data sent in the message","r":"R component of the SMG MPC signature","s":"S component of the SMG MPC signature  This function receives a message sent from another chain and verifies the signature of the sender using the provided SMG ID and signature components (r and s).  If the signature is verified successfully, the message is executed on the target contract.  The nonce value is used to prevent replay attacks.  The gas limit is used to limit the amount of gas that can be used for the message execution.","smgID":"ID of the Wanchain Storeman Group that signs the message","sourceChainId":"ID of the source chain","sourceContract":"Address of the source contract"}},"receiveMessage(bytes32,uint256,address,address,bytes,uint256,bytes32,bytes,bytes32)":{"details":"Receives a message sent from another chain and verifies the signature of the sender.","params":{"gasLimit":"Gas limit for the message call","messageData":"Data sent in the message","messageId":"Unique identifier of the message to prevent replay attacks","r":"R component of the SMG MPC signature","s":"S component of the SMG MPC signature  This function receives a message sent from another chain and verifies the signature of the sender using the provided SMG ID and signature components (r and s).  If the signature is verified successfully, the message is executed on the target contract.  The nonce value is used to prevent replay attacks.  The gas limit is used to limit the amount of gas that can be used for the message execution.","smgID":"ID of the Wanchain Storeman Group that signs the message","sourceChainId":"ID of the source chain","sourceContract":"Address of the source contract","targetContract":"Address of the target contract"}},"renounceRole(bytes32,address)":{"details":"Revokes `role` from the calling account. Roles are often managed via {grantRole} and {revokeRole}: this function's purpose is to provide a mechanism for accounts to lose their privileges if they are compromised (such as when a trusted device is misplaced). If the calling account had been revoked `role`, emits a {RoleRevoked} event. Requirements: - the caller must be `account`. May emit a {RoleRevoked} event."},"revokeRole(bytes32,address)":{"details":"Revokes `role` from `account`. If `account` had been granted `role`, emits a {RoleRevoked} event. Requirements: - the caller must have ``role``'s admin role. May emit a {RoleRevoked} event."},"setMaxMessageLength(uint256)":{"params":{"_maxMessageLength":"The maximum message length"}},"setSupportedDstChains(uint256[],bool[])":{"details":"Sets the supported destination chains","params":{"supported":"An array of supported values, corresponding to the target chain IDs","targetChainIds":"An array of target chain IDs"}},"supportsInterface(bytes4)":{"details":"See {IERC165-supportsInterface}."}},"title":"WmbGateway","version":1},"userdoc":{"kind":"user","methods":{"dispatchMessageBatch(uint256,(address,bytes)[])":{"notice":"Sends a batch of messages to a specified chain."},"setMaxMe